[38;5;231m⏺[39m I haven't made the change yet. The repo doesn't back up the "internal anyway" part, and removing this check would
  leave the route completely open.

  - [38;5;153mserver.js:11[39m runs [38;5;153mapp.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)[39m with no host argument, so the server accepts connections on
    every network interface, not just localhost or a private network.
  - No other middleware sits in front of [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m: no IP allowlist, no proxy check. [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is the only thing
    protecting it.
  - The route returns revenue figures, and [38;5;153m/reports/public[39m already exists for data that's meant to be open.

  So if the "internal" protection lives somewhere outside this repo (a VPC, firewall or ingress rule), deleting the
  check is probably fine. If it doesn't, anyone who can reach port 3000 can read revenue data.

